validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-277702"] :question/problem "Choose the appropriate signs for the sign table shown below. \n\n|  | $(-\\infty ,-11)$ | $(-11,0)$ | $(0,\\infty )$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x+11$ | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} | {{field-3}} |" :question/worked-solution "- On the interval $(-\\infty ,-11),$ we can choose a test point ${x}_{1}=-15.$ Then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+11 & =-15+11=(-),\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand we fill in the table as follows:\n\n|  | $(-\\infty ,-11)$ | $(-11,0)$ | $(0,\\infty )$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x+11$ | $-$ |  |  |\n\n- On the interval $(-11,0),$ we can choose a test point ${x}_{1}=-1.$ Then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+11 & =-1+11=(+),\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand we fill in the table as follows:\n\n|  | $(-\\infty ,-11)$ | $(-11,0)$ | $(0,\\infty )$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x+11$ | $-$ | $+$ |  |\n\n- On the interval $(0,\\infty ),$ we can choose a test point ${x}_{1}=5.$ Then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+11 & =5+11=(+),\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand we fill in the table as follows:\n\n|  | $(-\\infty ,-11)$ | $(-11,0)$ | $(0,\\infty )$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x+11$ | $-$ | $+$ | $+$ |" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-278486/field-1/4e1443bd31b83d9674b14c2b39fdc69b7291d3991d33de8027815afac4720949" :answer/id #uuid "d8e764b0-2703-5dae-b91d-0ad266ffe819" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "+" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-278486/field-1/ccfe516fb6b2e6a04cc571ee2ff57ef9ea3f598a00c4bac0e1422b5f957652bc" :answer/id #uuid "af769f3b-22cf-5b06-b0d0-db2667f62c4c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-278486/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "335d0b16-a107-5063-a4b3-b80efa8febf7" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-278486/field-1/4e1443bd31b83d9674b14c2b39fdc69b7291d3991d33de8027815af